--TEST--
a `tainted` URL at an outbound call offers `Core\Http::allowUrl` around it, a quick fix only and never a fix-all, because the launderer may throw, `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`, `rule:ide/a-quick-fix-is-a-diagnostics-own-suggestion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
tainted string $outside = "http://example.com/status";
var $a = Core\Http\Client::get($out<|>side);
--REQUEST--
codeAction
--EXPECT--
3:31-3:41 refactor.rewrite Put on separate lines -> "(\n    $outside,\n)"
3:32-3:40 quickfix pass it through `Core\Http::allowUrl` -> "Core\Http::allowUrl($outside)"
